cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NostOS in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "NostOS: a postAI Odyssey"
abstract: >-
  NostOS is an isometric 2D survival game and web-world, built as a single long
  vibe-coding project to test the limits of the vector medium. It wraps a 1990s
  digital surface (GeoCities pages, a Netscape browser, a Unix V7 laptop) around
  a backend generated by large language models, and casts the player as a
  critical code reader, rewarded for going into the source, the archives and the
  commit history. It carries an in-world Standard ML interpreter checked against
  a formal definition, and treats reading code as a game mechanic. A work of
  vector literature.
type: software
